  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/0ca9f7f2-e5be-4c01-a6f8-df8ce9489288-97701065-e1b4-4af1-a16d-56dd9884b1bf-image.png\" style=\"width: 273px; height: 249px;\" /></p><p>Use the formula&nbsp;of the gravitational potential in terms of universal gravitational constant,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow><mi>R</mi></mfrac></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>50</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>25</mn></mfrac></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>G</mi></math>.</p>",
